    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p24-q25-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find an expression for $f^{-1}(x)$ when $f(x)=\\frac{3x+7}{2x-8}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{8x+7}{2x-3}$, $x\\ne\\frac32$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{3x+7}{2x-8}\\\\x&=\\frac{3y+7}{2y-8}\\\\x(2y-8)&=3y+7\\\\2xy-8x&=3y+7\\\\(2x-3)y&=8x+7\\\\y&=\\frac{8x+7}{2x-3}\\\\f^{-1}(x)&=\\frac{8x+7}{2x-3}\\end{align*}$$\nThe original domain excludes $4$; its range excludes $\\frac32$. Thus the inverse has domain $\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{\\frac32\\}$ and range $\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{4\\}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 55
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q25-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find a general expression for $g^{-1}(x)$ when $g(x)=\\frac{ax+b}{cx+d}$. Assume $ad-bc\\ne0$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$g^{-1}(x)=\\frac{dx-b}{a-cx}$, where $a-cx\\ne0$ and $ad-bc\\ne0$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{ax+b}{cx+d}\\\\x&=\\frac{ay+b}{cy+d}\\\\x(cy+d)&=ay+b\\\\cxy+dx&=ay+b\\\\(a-cx)y&=dx-b\\\\y&=\\frac{dx-b}{a-cx}\\\\g^{-1}(x)&=\\frac{dx-b}{a-cx}\\end{align*}$$\nThe condition $ad-bc\\ne0$ ensures an inverse exists. The original domain is $\\{x\\in\\mathbb R:cx+d\\ne0\\}$, and the inverse domain is $\\{x\\in\\mathbb R:a-cx\\ne0\\}$. These are the inverse range and original range, respectively.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 58
      }
    ]
  },
